{"id":"00bd6f946aa1721c","group":"88","path":"88/88-df-church-turing-thesis.md","title":"Church-Turing Thesis (Metatheoretic)","display":"df-church-turing-thesis — Church-Turing Thesis (Metatheoretic)","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Computability and Logic","book_abbrev":"88","label":"88-df-church-turing-thesis","aliases":["88-df-church-turing-thesis"],"display":"df-church-turing-thesis — Church-Turing Thesis (Metatheoretic)","depends_on":["[[88-df-computable-function]]","[[88-df-partial-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Computability and Logic"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"88"},{"key":"label","html":"88-df-church-turing-thesis"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>88-df-church-turing-thesis</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-church-turing-thesis — Church-Turing Thesis (Metatheoretic)"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64279ecae5246baf\" href=\"?note=64279ecae5246baf\" title=\"88-df-computable-function\">88-df-computable-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d585cbf989199162\" href=\"?note=d585cbf989199162\" title=\"88-df-partial-function\">88-df-partial-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> (arity)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> (candidate partial function <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N\">\\(\\mathbb N^k\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb N\\)</span>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartialFunction}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartialFunction}\\)</span> (partial-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d585cbf989199162\" href=\"?note=d585cbf989199162\" title=\"88-df-partial-function\">88-df-partial-function</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\">\\(\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\\)</span> (由固定分类参数解释的谓词)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Comp}_k(f)\">\\(\\mathrm{Comp}_k(f)\\)</span> (Turing-computability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"64279ecae5246baf\" href=\"?note=64279ecae5246baf\" title=\"88-df-computable-function\">88-df-computable-function</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\">\\(\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\\)</span> (the metatheoretic Church--Turing thesis)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal E=(E_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb N}\">\\(\\mathcal E=(E_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb N}\\)</span> 是固定但不预先指定外延的分类参数族，满足\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;(E_k\\subseteq\\{f:\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\\})\">\\(\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;(E_k\\subseteq\\{f:\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\\})\\)</span>。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\">\\(\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\\)</span> 以下述成员关系解释；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\">\\(\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\\)</span> 是相对于同一固定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal E\">\\(\\mathcal E\\)</span> 的论题句。这里不假定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_k\">\\(E_k\\)</span> 等于可计算函数类，也不声称直观“有效方法”的外延已由其他文件唯一决定。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\">\\(\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\\)</span> 在本定义标签中只标记元语言的定义性引入，不表示论题句本身已经得到证明。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}church\\text{-}turing\\text{-}thesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\n\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall f\\quad\n\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\\leftrightarrow f\\in E_k\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}church\\text{-}turing\\text{-}thesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\n\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall f\\quad\n\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\\leftrightarrow f\\in E_k\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}church\\text{-}turing\\text{-}thesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\n\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\n\\coloneqq\n\\left[\n\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall f\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\n\\to\n(\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\n\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Comp}_k(f))\n\\Bigr)\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}church\\text{-}turing\\text{-}thesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{Meta}}\n\\mathsf{CT}_{88}\n\\coloneqq\n\\left[\n\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall f\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\n\\to\n(\\mathsf{EffComp}^{\\mathrm{pre}}_k(f)\n\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Comp}_k(f))\n\\Bigr)\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>本文件保留 Church--Turing 论题的比较结构：一个拟解释“有效方法”的分类，与正式 Turing 可计算性相比较。第一断言只使该分类成为有确定类型、相对于指定参数可解释的谓词；第二断言仍只是为论题句命名。</p>\n<p>未把 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_k\">\\(E_k\\)</span> 定义成可计算函数类，否则论题会被偷换为同义反复。也未用一个未解释的自然语言分类直接充当 Assertion 的已定义谓词。如何用实践中的直观方法解释该分类参数是论题的元理论内容，不是由本文件证明的数学事实。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"88-df-computable-function","status":"resolved","id":"64279ecae5246baf","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[